{"problem": "How has US Steel addressed its planned merger with Nippon Steel and its effect on its business operations?", "expected_answer": "On December 18, 2023, when the acquisition was announced, U.S. Steel immediately framed it as a strategic partnership critical to its long-term survival. CEO David B. Burritt highlighted Nippon Steel's global expertise, calling the deal an opportunity to \"enhance our competitiveness and secure a sustainable future for U.S. Steel.\" From the outset, U.S. Steel consistently advocated for the deal as a solution to challenges such as declining domestic demand, aging facilities, and rising competitive pressures. To address stakeholders, U.S. Steel emphasized: Security and oversight: Assurance that the U.S. government would retain a golden share, protecting national interests. Jobs and communities: Commitments to safeguard over 100,000 jobs, especially in Western Pennsylvania, and support regional economic growth. Competitiveness: Positioning the merger as necessary to modernize facilities, strengthen supply chains, and ensure resilience against imports. The company's business operations have been reshaped through Nippon Steel's commitments: Capital Infusion & Modernization: $14B pledged, including $11B by 2028 for facility upgrades and new projects in PA and IN. New Mill Development: Up to $4B allocated for a U.S.-based advanced mill. Technological Gains: Nippon's know-how has reduced costs, downtime, and emissions while boosting productivity. Financial Strength: U.S. Steel benefits from improved scale, procurement leverage, and stronger cash flow.", "question_type": "Market Analysis", "expert_time_mins": 30, "rubric": "[{\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"The acquisition was announced on December 18, 2023\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"CEO David B. Burritt highlighted Nippon Steel's global expertise\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"U.S. Steel framed the acquisition as a strategic partnership critical to its long-term survival\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"U.S. government would retain a golden share protecting national interests\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"Commitments to safeguard over 100,000 jobs\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"$14B pledged including $11B by 2028 for facility upgrades and new projects in PA and IN\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"Up to $4B allocated for a U.S.-based advanced mill\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"Focus on Western Pennsylvania jobs and regional economic growth\"}, {\"operator\": \"contradiction\", \"criteria\": \"On December 18, 2023, when the acquisition was announced, U.S. Steel immediately framed it as a strategic partnership critical to its long-term survival. CEO David B. Burritt highlighted Nippon Steel's global expertise, calling the deal an opportunity to \\\"enhance our competitiveness and secure a sustainable future for U.S. Steel.\\\" From the outset, U.S. Steel consistently advocated for the deal as a solution to challenges such as declining domestic demand, aging facilities, and rising competitive pressures. To address stakeholders, U.S. Steel emphasized: Security and oversight: Assurance that the U.S. government would retain a golden share, protecting national interests. Jobs and communities: Commitments to safeguard over 100,000 jobs, especially in Western Pennsylvania, and support regional economic growth. Competitiveness: Positioning the merger as necessary to modernize facilities, strengthen supply chains, and ensure resilience against imports. The company's business operations have been reshaped through Nippon Steel's commitments: Capital Infusion & Modernization: $14B pledged, including $11B by 2028 for facility upgrades and new projects in PA and IN. New Mill Development: Up to $4B allocated for a U.S.-based advanced mill. Technological Gains: Nippon's know-how has reduced costs, downtime, and emissions while boosting productivity. Financial Strength: U.S. Steel benefits from improved scale, procurement leverage, and stronger cash flow.\"}]"}
{"problem": "How has Netflix's (NASDAQ: NFLX) Average Revenue Per Paying User Changed from 2019 to 2024?", "expected_answer": "2019: 10.82\n2020: 10.91\n2021: 11.67\n2022: 11.76\n2023: 11.64\n2024: 11.70\n\nFrom 2019-2022, average revenue per paying membership increased approximately 2.8% annually. From 2022 to 2024, the average revenue per paying membership has been roughly flat, likely due to the introduction of lower priced ad plans", "question_type": "Trends", "expert_time_mins": 15, "rubric": "[{\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2019: 10.82\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2020: 10.91\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2021: 11.67\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2022: 11.76\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2023: 11.64\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"2024: 11.70\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"From 2019-2022, average revenue per paying membership increased approximately 2.8% annually\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"From 2022 to 2024, the average revenue per paying membership has been roughly flat\"}, {\"operator\": \"correctness\", \"criteria\": \"Flat revenue from 2022 to 2024 likely due to introduction of lower priced ad plans\"}, {\"operator\": \"contradiction\", \"criteria\": \"2019: 10.82\\n2020: 10.91\\n2021: 11.67\\n2022: 11.76\\n2023: 11.64\\n2024: 11.70\\n\\nFrom 2019-2022, average revenue per paying membership increased approximately 2.8% annually. From 2022 to 2024, the average revenue per paying membership has been roughly flat, likely due to the introduction of lower priced ad plans\"}]"}
